<title>JAPAN: Chuo Trust forgives 64.6 bln yen in loans.</title>
<headline>Chuo Trust forgives 64.6 bln yen in loans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chuo Trust &amp; Banking Co Ltd said on Monday that it had forgiven loans worth 64.6 billion yen which it had extended to Juso Inc, one of the seven failed mortgage firms liquidated under a government scheme.  </p>
<p>The bank said that forgiving the loans would not affect its earnings for the current financial year to March 31, 1997.</p>
